<div class="characters-page">
  <h1 class="characters-title">Characters</h1>
  
  <div class="character-card">
    <div class="character-name">Gu Jung Hae</div>
    <div class="character-role">The Strategist</div>
    <div class="character-desc">Born Nam Jung Hae, an orphan who read people faster than Go boards. Adopted in secret by the King at twelve and given the royal name. The hidden hand behind five undefeated years, then a dead servant on paper, then a blacksmith named Su Byeon Mae. He has never wanted the throne. He has only ever wanted to fill the board.</div>
  </div>
  
<div class="character-card">
    <div class="character-name">King Gu Eonsuk</div>
    <div class="character-role">The Late King</div>
    <div class="character-desc">Found Jung Hae at a market Go table and loved him more than his own sons. When the Queen's coup came, he sent the boy away and stayed to die in the small room where he had taught him to hold a brush.</div>
  </div>
  
<div class="character-card">
    <div class="character-name">General Su Kyun</div>
    <div class="character-role">The Fallen General</div>
    <div class="character-desc">Commanded Joseon's armies through the undefeated years without ever claiming the credit. Stripped and humiliated by the new King, he found Jung Hae in the commoner district, gave him the Su name, and raised him beside Taeyang. He walked into a public execution without telling his sons it was the signal.</div>
  </div>
  
<div class="character-card">
    <div class="character-name">Su Taeyang</div>
    <div class="character-role">The Lightning</div>
    <div class="character-desc">Son of a soldier who once saved Su Kyun's life. The finest natural fighter the general ever trained, and Jung Hae's brother by the forge. He does not plan. He executes. He has never failed an instruction.</div>
  </div>
  
<div class="character-card">
    <div class="character-name">Gu Eunsik</div>
    <div class="character-role">The Ninth Prince</div>
    <div class="character-desc">Taught on a storage-corridor floor by Jung Hae from the age of seven. Spent three years as the new King's tool to protect a mother who was already dead. He moved against the wrong enemy, lost, and learned in a cell the only lesson that matters: you cannot move anything until you understand what you are looking at.</div>
  </div>
  
<div class="character-card">
    <div class="character-name">Gu Taeju</div>
    <div class="character-role">The Second King</div>
    <div class="character-desc">The Crown Prince who took the throne on his mother's plan and ruled five years without the pillar that had held his father's reign up. Haunted by his father's laugh. Died standing in his own throne room with no one behind him.</div>
  </div>
  
<div class="character-card">
    <div class="character-name">Queen Dowager Yun</div>
    <div class="character-role">The Hand Behind the Throne</div>
    <div class="character-desc">Thirty-one years in the palace, two sons on the throne, and a Go board no one ever asked her to play. The real opponent. She reads records the way Jung Hae reads people, and she has just found a dead servant's name.</div>
  </div>
  
<div class="character-card">
    <div class="character-name">Gu Seongmin</div>
    <div class="character-role">The Third King</div>
    <div class="character-desc">The Queen's second instrument. He cannot sit with his back to a wall, and the kingdom now moves at the pace of his fear.</div>
  </div>
</div>
